\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 Implementation Prompt \'97 Reference: video_1.mp4\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 You are working on the existing native C++ Adobe After Effects plugin project, VHSart.\
Your task is to implement a dedicated visual preset that accurately reconstructs the supplied reference video:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Reference:
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  
\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 video_1.mp4
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Duration:
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  1.38 seconds\uc0\u8232 
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Preset Name:
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  
\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 Dense Colored Speckle & Soft Bleed
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 \
The reference is characterized by dense, small, highly saturated RGB speckle noise flickering across the entire frame, combined with subtle chromatic bleeding and a soft, low-resolution analog image base.\
This is NOT a tracking-tear effect, NOT a horizontal static-band effect, and NOT a geometric signal-collapse effect.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 1. Mandatory Project Audit Before Implementation\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Before writing or modifying code:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	1.	}Inspect the complete VHSart project structure.\
{\listtext	2.	}Identify all existing noise, static, grain, chroma, RGB separation, blur, softness, low-resolution, and signal-processing engines.\
{\listtext	3.	}Inspect their actual implementations, parameter ranges, rendering order, and current limitations.\
{\listtext	4.	}Determine whether the existing engines can reproduce the reference accurately through preset configuration and parameter extensions.\
{\listtext	5.	}Reuse and extend existing implementations wherever technically appropriate.\
{\listtext	6.	}Do not create duplicate engines for functionality already supported.\
{\listtext	7.	}If the existing noise engine cannot generate sufficiently fine, saturated, independently colored speckles, implement a dedicated Colored Speckle component that integrates into the existing noise architecture.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Do not assume an engine supports a feature simply because its UI contains a similarly named parameter. Verify its actual rendering behavior.\
Preserve all existing presets, engines, controls, and functionality.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 2. Reference Visual Identity\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Reconstruct these characteristics:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Dense, small, multicolored RGB speckles distributed across the entire frame.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Individual red, green, blue, cyan, yellow, orange, magenta, and occasional white speckles.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Strong chromatic saturation relative to the dark underlying image.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Continuous per-frame changes in speckle positions, colors, and distribution.\
{\listtext	\'95	}A soft, low-resolution analog image base.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Subtle chromatic bleeding across illuminated edges and colored regions.\
{\listtext	\'95	}A predominantly blue/indigo image character with warm orange/yellow highlights where present in the source footage.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The original image content must remain recognizable.\
The noise must cover the full image, including dark regions. Do not restrict it to highlights or edges unless an optional masking mode is explicitly enabled.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 3. Colored Speckle System\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Implement or extend a dedicated fine-grained colored-speckle generation component.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 Spatial generation\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Use a deterministic, fast hash-based random generator based on:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Pixel or sampling-cell X coordinate.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Pixel or sampling-cell Y coordinate.\
{\listtext	\'95	}User seed.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Temporal frame index or quantized time.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Generate a probability value for each sampling location:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 p = Hash(x, y, effectiveSeed)
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 \
Compare it against the normalized density parameter to determine whether a speckle is generated.\
Generate RGB colors independently or through a controlled saturated-color distribution. Avoid producing mostly neutral gray or white noise.\
The system must support:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Fine, near-pixel-sized speckles.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Optional slightly larger speckles.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Independent RGB color variation.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Adjustable saturation.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Adjustable brightness and opacity.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Configurable spatial distribution.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Stable deterministic output for the same seed and frame.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Different speckle patterns on successive frames when temporal flicker is enabled.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Avoid obvious repeated tiles, visible hash patterns, large blocks, or artificial grid structures.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 Required controls\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Colored Speckle Enable.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Speckle Density.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Speckle Size.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Speckle Saturation.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Speckle Brightness.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Speckle Opacity.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Speckle Flicker.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Temporal Variation / Animation Speed.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Random Seed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The Density control must genuinely affect the number of generated speckles, not merely increase their brightness.\
The Size control must change spatial dimensions without unexpectedly reducing density or changing the overall effect strength.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 4. Temporal Flicker and Determinism\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 The reference shows rapidly changing speckle patterns across successive frames.\
Implement a temporal seed system:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 effectiveSeed = Hash(userSeed, frameIndex)
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 \
Requirements:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Same seed and same frame must always produce identical output.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Different frames must generate changing speckle arrangements when flicker is enabled.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Disabling flicker must freeze the speckle pattern.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Changing the random seed must produce a different but visually consistent variation.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Animation Speed must control how frequently the random pattern changes.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Support deterministic rendering during timeline scrubbing and repeated renders.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Do not use uncontrolled global random state, wall-clock time, or thread-dependent random generation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Use the correct After Effects time/frame information and account for composition frame rate and render time.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 5. Soft Low-Resolution Base & Chroma Bleed\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Reuse VHSart\'92s existing softness and chroma-processing engines wherever possible.\
Implement the following visual behavior:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 Base Softness\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Apply subtle, controlled low-pass filtering to the original image to reduce high-frequency detail.\
Expose:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Base Softness.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Optional Low-Resolution Character.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Optional Fine Detail Preservation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Avoid excessive blur. The underlying scene must remain readable.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 Chroma Bleed\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Implement subtle chromatic spreading or channel-aware neighboring sampling.\
Expose:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Chroma Bleed.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Chroma Spread.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Optional RGB Channel Offset.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Keep this effect restrained by default. The reference has soft color transitions rather than aggressive RGB splitting or large directional smears.\
Do not introduce strong geometric distortion, horizontal tearing, vertical displacement, or unrelated tracking artifacts.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 6. Correct Rendering Order\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Use a rendering pipeline consistent with the existing VHSart architecture:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	1.	}Read and correctly interpret the original input frame.\
{\listtext	2.	}Apply the soft low-resolution base treatment.\
{\listtext	3.	}Apply subtle chroma bleeding.\
{\listtext	4.	}Generate and composite the colored speckle layer.\
{\listtext	5.	}Apply final output processing while preserving the intended noise detail.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The fine speckle layer must not be blurred away by the base-softness stage.\
If existing VHSart processing requires a different order, preserve its established architecture while ensuring the final visible result retains crisp, fine colored speckles over a soft underlying image.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 7. Preset Defaults\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Create the following initial preset configuration as a starting point for visual matching, not as claims of exact measured reference values:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls10\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Colored Speckle Density: 60%.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Speckle Size: 1.5 px.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Speckle Saturation: 80%.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Speckle Brightness: moderate to high.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Speckle Opacity: moderate to high.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Speckle Flicker: enabled.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Animation Speed: frame-responsive.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Base Softness: 45%.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Chroma Bleed: 35%.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Random Seed: deterministic default.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The user must be able to adjust every exposed parameter independently.\
Do not hardcode these values into the rendering algorithm.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 8. Preset Isolation and VHSart Integration\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Register the preset under the appropriate existing VHSart category.\
Display name:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Dense Colored Speckle & Soft Bleed
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
Reference identifier:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 video_1.mp4
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 \
Use the existing noise and chroma engines wherever possible. If a specialized speckle generator is required, integrate it as a reusable component rather than embedding all its logic directly inside the preset.\
Keep this preset visually independent from:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Tracking Noise.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Tracking Damage.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Snow.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Horizontal Static Bands.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Split-Band Chromatic Collapse.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Diagonal Sync Collapse.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Multi-Band Tracking Tear.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Other existing VHSart presets.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Do not automatically enable unrelated effects when this preset is selected.\
Preset selection should configure its intended parameters without destroying the user\'92s ability to customize them.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 9. Alpha, Pixel Formats, and Performance\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 The implementation must:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls12\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Preserve the original Alpha channel.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Respect premultiplied-alpha handling.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Avoid colored noise appearing outside transparent regions.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Handle different supported After Effects pixel formats correctly.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Avoid out-of-bounds memory access.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Avoid data races and shared mutable random state.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Remain safe under Multi-Frame Rendering.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Use deterministic per-frame random generation.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Avoid unnecessary full-frame allocations.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Keep the speckle generator efficient at high resolutions.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 For partially transparent pixels, composite noise according to the actual alpha coverage and the plugin\'92s established premultiplication conventions.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 10. Visual Validation\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Do not consider the feature complete merely because it compiles.\
Render the preset inside After Effects and compare it against the supplied 
\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 video_1.mp4
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 .\
Perform visual inspection at:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls13\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}100% scale.\
{\listtext	\'95	}200% scale.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Multiple successive frames.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Dark image regions.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Bright image regions.\
{\listtext	\'95	}High-resolution footage.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Validate the following:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls14\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	1.	}Speckles remain small and individually recognizable.\
{\listtext	2.	}RGB colors are clearly differentiated and saturated.\
{\listtext	3.	}Noise distribution covers the full frame.\
{\listtext	4.	}Temporal flicker changes the speckle pattern without introducing uncontrolled brightness pumping.\
{\listtext	5.	}Base softness remains subtle.\
{\listtext	6.	}Chroma bleed remains restrained.\
{\listtext	7.	}Original scene geometry remains stable.\
{\listtext	8.	}No unintended horizontal tracking bands or large tears appear.\
{\listtext	9.	}No obvious repeated patterns or spatial grids appear.\
{\listtext	10.	}Alpha and premultiplication remain correct.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Compare the reference and generated output using synchronized frames and consistent source footage whenever possible.\
Do not claim exact visual matching without actual rendered comparisons.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 11. Final Deliverables\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Provide:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls15\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	1.	}Complete implementation integrated into the existing VHSart project.\
{\listtext	2.	}Updated preset registration and UI controls.\
{\listtext	3.	}Reusable engine/component changes, with no unnecessary duplicated systems.\
{\listtext	4.	}Successful compilation and relevant automated tests.\
{\listtext	5.	}Actual After Effects render validation.\
{\listtext	6.	}A concise report describing:\cf2 \strokec2 \uc0\u8232 \u8232 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls15\ilvl1\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}Which existing engines were reused.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}Which engines or components were extended.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}Whether a dedicated speckle generator was necessary.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}Which tests passed.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}Any remaining visual differences from the reference.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Do not remove or break existing VHSart functionality.\
Do not replace real implementation with placeholder controls or UI-only parameters.\
The final result must be a functional, adjustable, procedural VHSart preset\'97not a pre-rendered overlay, texture image, GIF, or video layer.\
}